ok, this may have been suggested in some form before, I'm not sure but
apologies if it has!

my only problem with bones piles is the fact that a bones with several
(3+) artifacts has the potential to ruin a game. Say you are a Priest,
a conduct which is limited in many weapons, and you find a bones with
Grayswandir, Vorpal Blade, Stormbringer and Frost Brand. While they
may be of some use, none of them would be my first choice and the
presence of these, even if you destroy them or stick them in a chest,
makes obtaining anything else a LOT harder. Or, if you are trying a
game where you intend to wish for an artifact (atheist, naked,
etc...)

Would it be too extreme to suggest that in a bones pile, only one or
two artifacts randomly selected from however many the player was
carrying will survive, and the rest revert back to plain weapons/
whatever else? Or would this not meet with approval?

